bc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":39.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.012,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Viavi Solutions Inc. engages in the provision of test and measurement and optical technologies for military, aerospace, railway and first responder communications in the Americas, the Asia-Pacific, Europe, the Middle East, and Africa. The company operates in two segments, Network and Service Enablement (NSE) and Optical Security and Performance Products (OSP). The NSE segment provides integrated portfolio of test, monitoring, assurance, and resilient PNT solutions that enable and secure critical infrastructure. This segment also offers instruments, microprobes, and perpetual software licenses that support the development, production, maintenance, and optimization of network systems, as well as repair, calibration, extended warranty, software support, technical assistance, training, and consulting services. The OSP segment leverages its core optical coating technologies and volume manufacturing capability to design, manufacture, and sell technologies for the anti-counterfeiting, 3D sensing, government and aerospace, automotive, and industrial markets. The company was formerly known as JDS Uniphase Corporation. Viavi Solutions Inc. was founded in 1923 and is headquartered in Chandler, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Oleg  Khaykin | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $370K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Viavi Solutions Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $7.0B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 8-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 58% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $83M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 7.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 131% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3130615887717565},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-31.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $31.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 19% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Viavi Solutions (NASDAQ:VIAV) Stock Gets Price Target Cut from UBS Group","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/viavi-solutions-nasdaqviav-stock-gets-price-target-cut-from-ubs-group.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793971490.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Viavi Solutions (VIAV) Q1 2027 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/viavi-solutions-viav-q1-2027-191449000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906839.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"VIAV Q1 Earnings Beat Estimates on Data Center, A&D Strength","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/viav-q1-earnings-beat-estimates-144900927.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793890140.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"VIAV Q1 Earnings Call Maps New Data Center Test Markets","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/viav-q1-earnings-call-maps-140000